    "['access-list [parameter1] permit ip [parameter2] [parameter3] [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 then accept\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, ACLs are configured as firewall filters. The above creates:\\n1. A filter named ACL2001\\n2. A term called permit-192.168.1.0\\n3. Matches source address 192.168.1.0/24 (equivalent to 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255)\\n4. \"any\" destination is implied by not specifying a destination address\\n5. \"accept\" action is equivalent to \"permit\"', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 then accept', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 then accept', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco ACL command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 from source-address 192.168.1.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 then accept\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, ACLs are configured as firewall filters. The above creates:\\n1. A filter named ACL2001\\n2. A term called permit-192.168.1.0\\n3. Matches source address 192.168.1.0/24 (equivalent to 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255)\\n4. \"any\" destination is implied by not specifying a destination address\\n5. \"accept\" action is equivalent to \"permit\"', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.1.0 then accept'}]]": 1,
    "['access-list [parameter1] permit ip [parameter2] [parameter3] [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco access-list command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. Juniper uses firewall filters instead of access-lists\\n2. \"family inet\" specifies IPv4 processing\\n3. The filter is named ACL2001 to match the Cisco ACL number\\n4. The term \"permit-192.168.2.0\" is added to identify this specific rule\\n5. The source address 192.168.2.0/24 matches the Cisco version (192.168.2.0 with wildcard 0.0.0.255)\\n6. \"then accept\" is equivalent to \"permit\" in Cisco\\n7. The implicit \"any\" destination is handled by not specifying a destination address', 'trans_template': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco access-list command:\\n\\n##\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 from source-address 192.168.2.0/24\\nset firewall family inet filter ACL2001 term permit-192.168.2.0 then accept\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. Juniper uses firewall filters instead of access-lists\\n2. \"family inet\" specifies IPv4 processing\\n3. The filter is named ACL2001 to match the Cisco ACL number\\n4. The term 